:eedition.
:toc.
:body.
:h1 id=intro.Introduction
:p.This book is written in :hp2.BookMaster:ehp2. markup and formatted by
:hp1.bookie:ehp1., the VM/370plus formatter. The markup uses tags such as
&colon.p. and &colon.h1.; a symbol like &amp.colon. gives a colon.
:p.bookie knows:
:ul.
:li.headings, paragraphs and highlighting;
:li.ordered, unordered and simple lists, nested:
:ol.
:li.like this one,
:li.and this.
:eol.
:li.definition lists, screens, figures and tables.
:eul.
:h2.Definitions
:dl tsize=10.
:dt.CP
:dd.The Control Program: it gives every user a virtual machine.
:dt.CMS
:dd.The Conversational Monitor System, the single-user operating system
that runs in a virtual machine.
:edl.
:h2.A screen
:p.A command and its answer look like this:
:xmp.
bookie sample (ps
09:09:04 PUN FILE 0033  TO  MAINT    COPY 01 NOHOLD
09:09:24 PUN FILE 0034 FROM MAINT    COPY 01 NOHOLD
BOOKIE: SAMPLE PS A, 286 lines
Ready; T=0.19/0.23 09:09:24
:exmp.
:note.Screens keep their spacing.
:h1.Commands
:p.The formatters of VM/370plus:
:fig.
:table cols='10 10 30'.
:thd.
:row.
:c.Command
:c.Where
:c.What it does
:ethd.
:row.
:c.BOOKIE
:c.CMS
:c.Formats a BookMaster document in this style.
:row.
:c.TROFF
:c.CMS
:c.Formats a troff document with groff.
:row.
:c.PSPRINT
:c.CMS
:c.Prints PostScript, by spool or through the bridge.
:etable.
:figcap.The formatters
:efig.
:h2.Printing
:p.See :q.Introduction:eq. for the beginning. :attention.A PostScript
file must start with %!PS.
:euserdoc.
